  "chapter": 673,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 54 Chapter 673\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 1261-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the domestic relations law, in relation to allowing\n        for no fault separation\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  authorizes  separation between spouses if the relationship\nbetween the spouses has broken down irretrievably for  a  period  of  at\nleast  six  months,  conforming  to  existing  law  authorizing no fault\ndivorce. There are several technical issues  in  the  bill's  text  that\nwould  present  challenges for judicial interpretation and efficiency of\nproceedings.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact  changes  to\naddress  these  technical issues in the upcoming legislative session. On\nthe basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
